+  "impact": "src/http/handler.ts:31 mints the request id with `req.headers[\"x-request-id\"] ?? randomUUID()`. `??` only falls back on null/undefined, so a client sending an empty or whitespace-only `x-request-id` yields a blank id. Router.dispatch then calls AppLogger.withRequestId at src/http/router.ts:37, which throws \"AppLogger requires a non-empty request id\" before any route body runs, so app.handle rejects and the request 500s/crashes instead of being served under a fresh id. Fix: normalize at the boundary, e.g. `const raw = req.headers[\"x-request-id\"]; const requestId = raw !== undefined && raw.trim() !== \"\" ? raw : randomUUID()`. This does not conflict with r-p19bbvh0jhj8xgma, which constrains a job inheriting the enqueuing request's id, not how handler.ts mints an id for a request that supplied none. Found during T-2 plan review; pre-existing and out of scope for T-2, which touches src/jobs/.",
